WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.058 --> 00:00:04.000
The next morning Ally overslept.

2
00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:07.675
"Ack! I'm late for work!" She jumped out of bed.

3
00:00:07.676 --> 00:00:10.902
"Alpha, why didn't you wake me up as always?"

4
00:00:10.903 --> 00:00:13.425
Alpha made a snorting sound.

5
00:00:13.426 --> 00:00:16.105
"Ask your other phone to wake you up!"

6
00:00:16.106 --> 00:00:28.294
"I don't have another phone," Ally tried to say, but Alpha had shut herself down.

7
00:00:28.295 --> 00:00:33.221
At work, Barry had taken all the customers' orders.

8
00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:36.444
"Thanks for covering for me," Ally said.

9
00:00:36.445 --> 00:00:40.921
"No problem," Barry said. "I heard about your fundraiser for the soccer club.

10
00:00:40.922 --> 00:00:45.058
I'd love to help. Maybe I can cook something for you to sell?"

11
00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:48.093
"We're selling T-shirts, but thanks anyway."

12
00:00:48.094 --> 00:00:52.155
Ally started to refill the saltshakers when she got an idea.

13
00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:56.105
"Actually, I could use your help with something else.

14
00:00:56.106 --> 00:00:58.682
Can you meet me at Ray's house tonight?"

15
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:08.524
"Sure!" Barry looked so happy to be included, Ally couldn't help smiling too.

16
00:01:08.525 --> 00:01:13.596
Later Ally went to the print shop to look at some sample soccer T-shirts.

17
00:01:13.597 --> 00:01:17.244
"These look amazing, Eli!" Ally said.

18
00:01:17.245 --> 00:01:21.668
"Great. I'll start printing the rest of them right now," Eli said.

19
00:01:21.669 --> 00:01:25.480
Ally slipped one of the T-shirts over her clothes.

20
00:01:25.481 --> 00:01:32.644
"I can't wait to show Mateo! See you later. Thanks."

21
00:01:32.645 --> 00:01:35.861
Outside, she ran into Mayor Clark.

22
00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:40.841
"Nice T-shirt. Did Eli make that for you?" the mayor asked.

23
00:01:40.842 --> 00:01:45.436
"Yes. We're going to sell them to raise money for a soccer club."

24
00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:48.682
"Where will the club meet?" Mayor Clark asked.

25
00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:52.018
"At the soccer field in town," Ally said.

26
00:01:52.019 --> 00:01:55.985
"Oh!" The mayor got a funny look on her face.

27
00:01:55.986 --> 00:01:59.103
"The city just signed a contract with a developer.

28
00:01:59.104 --> 00:02:02.282
We're going to turn that field into a parking lot."

29
00:02:02.283 --> 00:02:07.278
"What?" Ally gasped. "Why?"

30
00:02:07.279 --> 00:02:13.928
"With more tourists coming to Sandville—thanks in large part to you, Ally—we need more parking lots.

31
00:02:13.929 --> 00:02:16.667
I've got a meeting. Nice to see you!"

32
00:02:16.668 --> 00:02:19.508
Ally stared after the mayor.

33
00:02:19.509 --> 00:02:22.104
"What have I done?" she thought.

34
00:02:22.105 --> 00:02:27.264
"I helped Sandville but totally wrecked Mateo's soccer club dreams!

35
00:02:27.265 --> 00:02:30.409
I can't believe the field is going to be destroyed.

36
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:34.698
And Eli is about to print a bunch more T-shirts!"

37
00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:38.907
Ally raced back to the shop to stop the order.

38
00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.838
But there was an Out to Lunch sign on the door.

39
00:02:41.839 --> 00:02:46.750
Ally reached for Alpha. Maybe she could call the shop and leave a message for Eli.

40
00:02:46.751 --> 00:02:50.501
But she'd left Alpha—who was really mad at her—at home.

41
00:02:50.502 --> 00:02:56.010
Ally groaned. "I'd better go tell Mateo about all this."

42
00:02:56.011 --> 00:03:00.228
Ally raced to the soccer field as fast as she could.

43
00:03:00.229 --> 00:03:04.932
When she got there, Coach and Mateo were on the field.

44
00:03:04.933 --> 00:03:09.181
"I dread telling them the bad news," Ally thought.

45
00:03:09.182 --> 00:03:12.019
"Hey, are you space girl?" someone called.

46
00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:18.072
Ally spun around. A boy, another soccer player, stood grinning at her.

47
00:03:18.073 --> 00:03:23.480
"Oh no!" Ally thought. "He knows I'm an alien!"

48
00:03:23.481 --> 00:03:30.205
"Hi, I'm Julius. You're the one who won the spot on Lainie Polk's P.O.D., right?"

49
00:03:30.206 --> 00:03:34.941
Ally laughed from relief. "Yes!"

50
00:03:34.942 --> 00:03:40.746
"It's so cool," Julius said. "You'll have to tell me all about space when you get back."

51
00:03:40.747 --> 00:03:43.758
"Oh, I . . ." Ally was stumped.

52
00:03:43.759 --> 00:03:46.770
She couldn't tell him she wasn't coming back to Earth.

53
00:03:46.771 --> 00:03:50.093
Then she remembered what Mateo had said about fibs.

54
00:03:50.094 --> 00:03:54.822
They weren't bad if no one got hurt.

55
00:03:54.823 --> 00:04:00.505
"Sure! I'll tell you all about space. Right now I'm waiting for Mateo.

56
00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:04.754
I have to tell him something. It's not about space, though."

57
00:04:04.755 --> 00:04:11.001
Julius pointed to a bench. "You can wait there. He'll be done soon."

58
00:04:11.002 --> 00:04:15.344
Ally blushed as Julius flashed her another smile.

59
00:04:15.345 --> 00:04:22.814
"His eyes are so blue," she thought.

60
00:04:22.815 --> 00:04:26.006
Soon Mateo and Coach trotted off the field.

61
00:04:26.007 --> 00:04:32.447
Mateo smiled when he saw Ally's shirt. "The T-shirt looks great!"

62
00:04:32.448 --> 00:04:39.828
"Yes, but . . ." Ally told them about her conversation with Mayor Clark.

63
00:04:39.829 --> 00:04:45.097
Mateo gasped. "This is terrible!"

64
00:04:45.098 --> 00:04:48.581
"Good thing you didn't get all the T-shirts printed," Coach said.

65
00:04:48.582 --> 00:04:54.079
Ally explained how she tried to cancel the print job, but Eli was out to lunch.

66
00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:57.074
"Excuse me." Julius stepped closer.

67
00:04:57.075 --> 00:04:59.336
"I couldn't help but overhear you.

68
00:04:59.337 --> 00:05:03.666
Don't cancel those T-shirts—we need to fight for our soccer field.

69
00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:08.174
And those shirts are a great way for Sandville residents to support us."

70
00:05:08.175 --> 00:05:11.013
"I agree!" Mateo said.

71
00:05:11.014 --> 00:05:14.619
"We could also write letters to the mayor," Julius said.

72
00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:19.325
"Maybe we could get people to sign a petition too," Mateo said.

73
00:05:19.326 --> 00:05:24.159
"Everyone at soccer camp will help us get signatures," Julius said.

74
00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.660
Ally grinned. "Let's do it!

75
00:05:26.661 --> 00:05:34.890
I really want to fix this before I leave for home—I mean, leave for space—with Lainie Polk!"

